        {
          "_key": "b-05-p-scope-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "An engineering deep dive into consumer reliability: navigating at-least-once delivery, eliminating dual-writes with the Transactional Outbox, and enforcing idempotent consumption.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-callout-note",
      "_type": "callout",
      "tone": "note",
      "title": "EIP Part 6 \u2014 Upcoming Series Installment",
      "items": [
        {
          "_key": "note-item-5",
          "title": "This architectural deep dive is currently in active development as part of the 8-part Enterprise Integration Patterns series on wiki.eiakoji.me. The formal theoretical derivations, Excalidraw-style schematics, Little's Law/queueing equations, and production Java 21 reference implementations will land directly in this publication entry.",
          "status": "upcoming"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-h2-patterns",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-05-h2-patterns-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "2. Pattern Catalog & Formal Realizations",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-p-patterns-intro",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-05-p-patterns-intro-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "In this installment, we formalize the following core integration patterns established by Gregor Hohpe and Bobby Woolf, mapping each to its modern cloud-native realization:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-pat-00",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-05-pat-00-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Messaging Gateway: Encapsulates broker communication APIs behind pure domain interfaces, isolating business logic from messaging drivers.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-pat-01",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-05-pat-01-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Transactional Client & Outbox: Atomic dual-write prevention: writes domain entities and outbound events to the same relational database transaction, publishing via CDC (Debezium).",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-pat-02",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-05-pat-02-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Polling Consumer vs Event-Driven Consumer: Contrasting pull-based batch retrieval with push-based reactive event loop thread dispatch.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-pat-03",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-05-pat-03-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Competing Consumers: Horizontal worker scaling where multiple consumer instances process messages concurrently from a shared queue or partition.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-pat-04",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-05-pat-04-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Idempotent Receiver: Guarantees that duplicate message delivery produces identical system state using unique token deduplication fences.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-pat-05",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-05-pat-05-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Selective Consumer & Durable Subscriber: Filtered queue polling combined with persistent consumer group offset tracking surviving client restarts.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-pat-06",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-05-pat-06-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Service Activator: Connects messages arriving on a channel to operations on domain services, returning execution output to reply channels.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-h2-invariants",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-05-h2-invariants-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "3. Invariants, Failure Modes & Physical Constraints",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-p-invariants-intro",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-05-p-invariants-intro-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Engineering resilient enterprise integration topologies requires analyzing the exact failure boundaries and physical constraints governing these patterns:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-inv-00",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-05-inv-00-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "The Dual-Write Dilemma: Updating a database and publishing to a message broker in separate steps guarantees eventual inconsistency; the Transactional Outbox is the foundational mechanism for atomic consistency.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-inv-01",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-05-inv-01-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "At-Least-Once Reality: In physical networks, distributed acknowledgments can fail; every production consumer must either execute idempotent mutations or maintain unique deduplication state.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_key": "b-05-inv-02",
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "b-05-inv-02-s0",
          "_type": "span",
          "text": "Poison Pill Quarantine: Messages that crash consumers on unhandled runtime exceptions must be routed to Dead Letter Channels before consuming worker retry budgets and causing pipeline blockage.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    }
  ]
}